{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">go get github.com/donseba/go-partial</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Recommended setup</h2>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root := partial.New("shell.gohtml").
    SetConnector(connector.NewHTMX(nil)).
    SetFileSystem(os.DirFS("web")).
    UseTemplateCache(true).
    Use(exterrors.Stage(exterrors.WithMode(exterrors.ModeDetailed)))</code></pre>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">During development you can leave template caching off. In production, cache parsed templates and keep data request-scoped. The root's cache setting applies to every partial rendered under it that does not set one itself, so <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">UseTemplateCache(!development)</code> on the root covers both. Error output defaults to safe mode; opt into detailed mode for local development diagnostics.</p>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Run <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">root.CheckTemplates()</code> when the application starts to find templates that would fail their renders, such as calls of functions the root does not have.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Template structure</h2>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">web/
  shell.gohtml
  header.gohtml
  pages/
    home.gohtml
    settings.gohtml</code></pre>
</article>

